From b82cb202219b1e46538cbcaaad3c65ed93b0843f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:13:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 234/258] fix(execution): reject self-consistent forged view
 decisions in plan and report

Independent verification showed that a forged layout_decision with recomputed
alias-proof and plan digests could be accepted and executed, because nothing
re-verified the proof digest, the proof facts, the obligation invariants, the
rule trace or the registered contract.

- add pypto.execution.layout_verify: recomputable alias-proof digest check,
  proof-facts/obligation agreement, must_not_alias/require/view/materialized
  invariants, rule/decision agreement, and canonical re-derivation from the
  frozen policy plus the registered OpDefinition
- ExecutionPlan.validate rejects content-local inconsistencies (including a
  mismatched rule trace) before any provider is selected
- entry._execute cross-checks the frozen decision against the matmul
  OpDefinition and the canonical decision; a self-consistent forgery is
  refused with ARTIFACT_MISMATCH and no provider is invoked
- validate_report_schema applies the same checks to the report copy, with the
  runtime alias_check=verified_distinct included
- tests: replay the verifier's plan/report tamper matrix plus recomputed-digest
  forgeries; both must be refused, the forged plan must not execute
